        "original_id": "82e5a2af-008f-5878-84c0-ec03b2c7d7b0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Phoenix, Arizona\n- Roads: Arizona State Route 51, Piestewa Freeway\n- People: Lori Piestewa\n- Organizations: U.S. military, Hopi tribe\n- Topics: highway naming, military service\n\nFacts:\n- Arizona State Route 51, also known as the Piestewa Freeway, is a numbered state highway in Phoenix, Arizona.\n- Lori Piestewa was a member of the Hopi tribe.\n- Lori Piestewa was the first Native American woman in history to die in combat while serving in the U.S. military.\n- Lori Piestewa was the first woman in the U.S. military killed in the Iraq War.\n- A peak was named after Lori Piestewa.",
